  "result": "I added `split(cents, parts)` to `shop/money.py`, and all 12 tests pass, including 6 new ones in `tests/test_money.py`.\n\nIt divides `cents` by `parts`, then adds one extra cent to each of the first parts until the remainder is used up:\n- `split(1000, 3)` gives `[334, 333, 333]`.\n- `split(2, 4)` gives `[1, 1, 0, 0]`.\n- A `parts` value below 1 raises `ValueError`.\n\nThe new tests cover even splits, remainders going to the first elements, more parts than cents, a single part, totals always matching `cents`, and the `ValueError` case.\n\nNegative amounts aren't tested. They still add up correctly, but the first parts come out less negative: `split(-5, 2)` gives `[-2, -3]`. If you want refunds to put the bigger amount first instead (`[-3, -2]`), that's a one-line change.",
